WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.040
Hey, what up? It's ya boy. Too depressed to work, so I filled this bag with Taco Bell. Let's go spoil Endgame.

00:00:09.140 --> 00:00:16.080
Alright. So, the first step for spoiling Endgame is you want to have at least a reasonable understanding of what happens in the movie.

00:00:16.080 --> 00:00:19.020
And the most efficient way of accomplishing that...

00:00:19.020 --> 00:00:21.320
is to just go see it.

00:00:21.840 --> 00:00:25.260
So, I guess that's the next step.

00:00:28.980 --> 00:00:33.920
So, this is possibly the weirdest thing to gripe about, but they changed the ticket printer,

00:00:33.920 --> 00:00:39.960
and they're just--they're so long now. Like, look how long these tickets are! It's as long as my hand.

00:00:39.960 --> 00:00:44.600
Alright, next step: try to make sure you get a somewhat reasonable seat.

00:00:45.560 --> 00:00:53.780
[Wholesome stock music plays] 3 HOURS LATER

00:00:53.880 --> 00:00:58.460
Alright, now that you've seen Infinity War, you're ready to spoil it, but you're already at the mall.

00:00:58.460 --> 00:01:02.260
So, you might as well go, like, get a hoodie or something.

00:01:04.800 --> 00:01:11.920
Okay, so, first off, I just want to warn you that Endgame is full of a ton of spoilers for...

00:01:12.120 --> 00:01:19.120
Avengers: Endgame, so, if you don't want to be spoiled on Endgame, don't go see Avengers: Endgame. It's, like, just...

00:01:19.120 --> 00:01:21.280
...wall to wall spoilers.

00:01:21.280 --> 00:01:27.920
Y'know, I'm just gonna say it doesn't matter how depressed you are, if your brain tells you to get 10 burritos...

00:01:27.980 --> 00:01:32.100
Don't do it. So, if you just want to be able to talk about Endgame,

00:01:32.100 --> 00:01:38.600
but you don't want to have to deal with the burden of details,

00:01:38.600 --> 00:01:43.080
then your main talking points are going to be about how...

00:01:43.080 --> 00:01:49.940
introspective the first hour is, how fan-servicey the last hour is, and...

00:01:50.340 --> 00:01:58.720
the great use of wide shots. There's some very well-composed wide shots, and...

00:01:58.720 --> 00:02:04.560
beats in the movie, and so, like, if you just kind of take those three...

00:02:04.780 --> 00:02:07.200
vague talking points and just...

00:02:08.100 --> 00:02:13.000
ramble about how, like, "Oh man, you know, I really did like how...

00:02:13.200 --> 00:02:17.800
introspective the first hour is, like, it was really -

00:02:18.120 --> 00:02:22.760
- really had the characters, like, look inside themselves and...

00:02:22.760 --> 00:02:26.720
grapple with sort of the meaning of things."

00:02:26.780 --> 00:02:31.080
Y'know, if you just riff like that for a good five minutes,

00:02:31.080 --> 00:02:34.940
you can convince anyone that you actually saw the movie.

00:02:34.940 --> 00:02:39.240
I want to keep going, but it's way too hot in my car, and I'm right next to a highway.

00:02:39.240 --> 00:02:43.280
So, if I open my window, there's gonna be way too much noise, so...

00:02:43.280 --> 00:02:47.860
let's - let's go home and do this.

00:02:47.860 --> 00:02:57.000
[Soft cutesy pet voice] Hey Amy, come here...come here Amy. Yeah, come here. There we go, there's Amy.

00:02:57.000 --> 00:02:59.600
That's Amy's side.

00:03:08.600 --> 00:03:10.900
[Whispers] Aww, there's an Amy.

00:03:12.940 --> 00:03:18.600
Now, if you don't want to be burdened with details, but you want to sound like you can talk about the movie,

00:03:18.600 --> 00:03:22.440
but you don't want to sound, like, super positive,

00:03:22.440 --> 00:03:29.040
then your core talking points are going to be that, like, the middle of the movie is just...

00:03:29.040 --> 00:03:30.900
like, kind of...

00:03:33.320 --> 00:03:39.040
...there. It's just a lot of make-work and a lot of it doesn't really have, you know,

00:03:39.940 --> 00:03:45.220
stakes or complications that come back in any meaningful way;

00:03:45.800 --> 00:03:52.660
that Captain Marvel is integrated into the film in a really...

00:03:53.720 --> 00:03:56.300
inelegant way; and...

00:03:58.040 --> 00:04:07.120
that for a huge chunk of the movie, they basically push every female character off-screen,

00:04:07.120 --> 00:04:14.000
but then, they all get a giant, like, action group shot together, and I guess that's supposed to make it all okay.

00:04:14.000 --> 00:04:21.160
That it's, like, well, "Hey, look, they get a big moment of badass". It's like a yearbook photo of...

00:04:21.160 --> 00:04:24.740
of kick-ass female characters.

00:04:25.340 --> 00:04:33.300
Sorry only one and a half of them got actual emotional development during the film itself.

00:04:33.300 --> 00:04:39.080
So, if you're looking for the kind of raw spoilers that you're going to, like, shout out the window of a car -

00:04:39.080 --> 00:04:45.160
- the main ones would be that Thanos gets punked in, like, the first 10 minutes of the movie;

00:04:45.420 --> 00:04:50.600
Black Widow dies; Iron Man dies; and...

00:04:50.900 --> 00:04:53.840
Captain America gets old and retires.

00:04:54.020 --> 00:04:58.260
So, those are gonna be your four main, like,

00:04:58.700 --> 00:05:05.480
things that people are gonna be, like, the most sensitive about because they're, you know,

00:05:06.220 --> 00:05:09.300
twists, or major plot developments,

00:05:10.460 --> 00:05:14.620
or whatnot. Hey, Amy, what are you getting into over there?

00:05:15.040 --> 00:05:18.560
Hey, Amy, what are you getting into? Amy...

00:05:19.020 --> 00:05:20.760
Amy...

00:05:28.500 --> 00:05:33.360
Sitting through the movie and going through it, it was very well constructed,

00:05:33.360 --> 00:05:40.740
and it was an enjoyable ride, and I had a good time, and it was emotionally satisfying, but...

00:05:41.760 --> 00:05:45.800
kind of insubstantial. Like, it's been...

00:05:46.540 --> 00:05:48.400
an hour, and...

00:05:48.400 --> 00:05:55.300
a bit since I got out of the movie and, already, I feel like I've moved on.

00:05:55.840 --> 00:05:59.560
Like, I'm - I'm -- I'm done.

00:06:00.580 --> 00:06:07.160
In a certain way, there's actually kind of this catharsis. Because, it's like the core -

00:06:07.160 --> 00:06:12.580
- the MCU that has been just...

00:06:13.200 --> 00:06:16.220
...bloating and...

00:06:17.440 --> 00:06:21.660
...building for the last decade, twenty-some-odd...

00:06:22.060 --> 00:06:26.740
movies, it's like, "Okay, it's over."

00:06:27.160 --> 00:06:29.160
"We are free!"

00:06:29.900 --> 00:06:33.160
So, how the plot ends up playing out is that,

00:06:34.060 --> 00:06:42.520
basically, the Avengers can't just fix the problem and...

00:06:43.180 --> 00:06:48.900
completely undo the first movie. So, what they do is a time heist.

00:06:48.900 --> 00:06:52.180
They build a time machine, go back in time,

00:06:52.720 --> 00:06:56.860
steal the Infinity Stones from various points in the previous movies,

00:06:56.860 --> 00:07:00.980
with the promise that they're gonna come back and, like, return them.

00:07:00.980 --> 00:07:02.840
Kind of like:

00:07:03.540 --> 00:07:07.380
"We'll be back in a minute! Like, one minute after we take the stones,

00:07:07.380 --> 00:07:11.800
we'll just show up and put them back, and it'll all be good!". And....uh

00:07:13.100 --> 00:07:16.300
Y'know, and through this,

00:07:16.300 --> 00:07:23.480
Past Thanos ends up getting alerted to their plan. And so, the big showdown at the end of the movie...

00:07:24.480 --> 00:07:25.680
after...

00:07:26.920 --> 00:07:32.720
everyone has been "unsnapped", is a showdown between...

00:07:34.040 --> 00:07:42.300
all the heroes and a past version of Thanos. So, you have everybody getting revenge on...

00:07:42.340 --> 00:07:47.040
the same dude, a...dude

00:07:47.040 --> 00:07:50.420
who has not yet done the thing...

00:07:50.640 --> 00:07:54.620
that you're getting revenge on him for. Even though he, like,

00:07:54.620 --> 00:07:57.900
personality-wise, has 100 percent confirmed that...

00:07:57.900 --> 00:08:00.900
He would do the same thing again, and is in fact

00:08:01.280 --> 00:08:06.920
actively trying to accomplish exactly the thing - like he still needs to be stopped.

00:08:06.929 --> 00:08:13.300
He is still trying to get the gauntlet and, like, snap everyone and also as far as he's concerned --

00:08:14.140 --> 00:08:17.900
-- well, I guess because it's now in a -- he's trying to like...

00:08:18.000 --> 00:08:20.200
...redo it.

00:08:20.200 --> 00:08:27.640
But anyway, like I feel like a bunch of the meat is taken out of it by the fact that like this Thanos...

00:08:28.660 --> 00:08:31.940
...doesn't know any of these people,

00:08:32.620 --> 00:08:35.040
and hasn't see them before.

00:08:35.040 --> 00:08:37.400
And there's even a moment that calls attention to this.

00:08:37.400 --> 00:08:40.500
Where like -- so Scarlet Witch, after she gets unsnapped,

00:08:40.500 --> 00:08:42.460
she gets a little one-on-one duel

00:08:42.460 --> 00:08:46.100
with Thanos, and she's like "You took everything from me!"

00:08:46.220 --> 00:08:49.160
Because Vision doesn't come back, 'cause Vision got killed not snapped.

00:08:49.180 --> 00:08:51.400
So, Vision is still dead.

00:08:52.120 --> 00:08:59.420
So, she's like "You took everything from me!" and he's just like..."I don't know who you are."

00:09:00.340 --> 00:09:06.400
And she's like "You will!" - and I thought that was gonna be a setup for her like,

00:09:06.520 --> 00:09:11.060
for like a moment where she uses her powers to like...

00:09:11.800 --> 00:09:17.340
Show him the consequences of what he did...

00:09:20.340 --> 00:09:26.600
But no, they just -- they just punch each other...

00:09:28.780 --> 00:09:36.900
I'm just gonna sit here and eat the remainder of all of these.

